# Userflow: upload a real fixture, create a one-step pipeline, start a job
# against the uploaded file, watch progress over SSE, then confirm COMPLETE.
# Precondition: full `pnpm dev` stack (orchestrator + Go worker actually
# consuming NATS dispatch messages + MinIO) — this is the one flow that needs
# the whole pipeline to run for real, not just the orchestrator + Postgres.
# Run: cd apps/orchestrator && pnpm test:http
#  or: httpyac send test/http/job-single-flow.http --all

@ORCHESTRATOR_URL = http://localhost:3000

# @name presign
POST {{ORCHESTRATOR_URL}}/uploads/presign
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "filename": "gradient.jpg",
  "contentType": "image/jpeg"
}

?? status == 201

###

# @ref presign
PUT {{presign.uploadUrl}}
Content-Type: image/jpeg

< ../../../../workers/testdata/images/gradient.jpg

?? status == 200

###

# @name pipeline
POST {{ORCHESTRATOR_URL}}/pipelines
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "job-single-flow-smoke",
  "steps": [
    { "id": "root", "processor": "image.resize", "params": { "width": 640, "height": 480 } }
  ]
}

?? status == 201

###

# Stacking two @ref lines on one request is confirmed working (verified live
# against a running orchestrator — both `presign` and `pipeline` resolve).
# @name job
# @ref presign
# @ref pipeline
POST {{ORCHESTRATOR_URL}}/jobs
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "pipelineId": "{{pipeline.id}}",
  "inputRef": "{{presign.objectKey}}"
}

?? status == 201
# No assertion on parsedBody.status here: JobsService.create() calls
# dispatchNext() *before* returning, so by the time this response arrives the
# worker may already have moved the job past QUEUED into RUNNING or even
# COMPLETE for a fixture this small — confirmed live, asserting QUEUED here
# is flaky. The terminal-state assertion below is the real check.

###

# Watch-and-print only — httpyac's documented SSE hook waits a fixed duration
# rather than inspecting individual frames (see design note in
# docs/tasks/TASK-orchestrator-http-userflow-tests.md). The real pass/fail
# assertion is the request below, not this one. Disabled by default:
# confirmed live that once the job is already terminal by the time this
# connects (typical for these tiny fixtures), the EventSource client
# auto-reconnects after the server closes the stream and gets 400s, which
# httpyac counts as a failed request and would trip --bail in
# `pnpm test:http`. Delete the @disabled line below to watch it by hand.
# @disabled
# @ref job
SSE {{ORCHESTRATOR_URL}}/jobs/{{job.id}}/events
Event: message

{{@streaming
  async function waitForJob(){
    await sleep(8000);
  }
  exports.waitPromise = waitForJob();
}}

###

# Deterministic wait for the worker to finish, instead of relying on the
# (disabled, unreliable) SSE step above.
# @sleep 5000
# @ref job
GET {{ORCHESTRATOR_URL}}/jobs/{{job.id}}

?? status == 200
?? js response.parsedBody.status == COMPLETE
